rocess control agent. The alloy powders were deposited over an Inconel 718 substrate by air plasma spraying (APS) to form overlay coatings. Heat treatment at 1200 \u00baC during 3 h in vacuum was conducted to homogenize the coating and improve the adhesion by diffusion between the substrate and the coating. Subsequent oxidation treatment at 1100 \u00baC for 5 h was carried out to allow the formation of oxides scales. X-ray diffraction patterns were obtained of the as-milled powders as well as of the coatings. Microstructural evolution of samples were also analyzed by scanning electron microscopy (SEM).\n    Fecha de publicaci\u00f3n: 2011\n    Tipo de publicaci\u00f3n: P\u00f3ster de congreso\n    Idioma: Ingl\u00e9s\n    \u00c1rea de conocimiento: F\u00cdSICA\n    Colecciones: Art\u00edculos de Congresos": [0.0, 0.08770579844713211, 0.0, 0.0, 0.35082319378852844, 0.08770579844713211, 0.0, 0.08770579844713211, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.13155870139598846, 0.0, 0.21926450729370117, 0.08770579844713211, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.17541159689426422, 0.043852899223566055, 0.13155870139598846, 0.043852899223566055, 0.08770579844713211, 0.0, 0.08770579844713211, 0.13155870139598846, 0.0, 0.0, 0.08770579844713211, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.13155870139598846, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.0, 0.08770579844713211, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.13155870139598846, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.13155870139598846, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.0, 0.43852901458740234, 0.043852899223566055, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.08770579844713211, 0.043852899223566055, 0.13155870139598846, 0.043852899223566055, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.08770579844713211, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.21926450729370117, 0.08770579844713211, 0.17541159689426422, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.13155870139598846, 0.13155870139598846, 0.0, 0.0, 0.13155870139598846, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.08770579844713211, 0.13155870139598846, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.13155870139598846, 0.0, 0.08770579844713211, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.17541159689426422, 0.0, 0.13155870139598846, 0.0, 0.0, 0.13155870139598846, 0.0, 0.043852899223566055, 0.0, 0.26311740279197693, 0.08770579844713211, 0.08770579844713211, 0.0], "T\u00edtulo: Pellets from forest waste: A viable alternative fuel in Mexico\n    Autores: IGNACIO MARTIN MONICA MORENO LOPEZ MARIA TERESA ALARCON HERRERA\n    Colaboradores: \n    Nivel de acceso: Acceso Abierto\n    Licencia: Sin Derechos Reservados\n    Materia: Wood pellets Biofuel\n    Resumen: The search for non-fossil fuels is a task of global interest. In the case of Mexican forest waste (sawdust,\nsplinters, and woodchips), it is estimated that 45% of this biomass is discarded as garbage rather than used industrially.\nThe production of wood pellets is a viable alternative for the recovery of wooden waste from wood processing, forestry,\nand other industrial uses (such as the wooden pallets used with forklifts for the transport and storage of manufactured\ngoods). Wood pellets are compressed cylinders between 6 and 10mm in diameter, used for generating thermal energy.\nThe increase in European pellet consumption has promoted the construction of many pelletizing plants in that continent,\nand this trend has extended to Africa, North America, and South America. In Mexico, however, this industry does not yet\nexist despite the fact that 72% of the national territory is dedicated to various forestry uses. The State of Chihuahua,\nlocated in northern Mexico, has the second largest timber production in the country. This research project encompassed\nthe 10 most significant sawmills in the region of Ciudad Madera, Chihuahua. Their timber resources and their generation\nrates were analyzed and quantified. The purpose of this project was to determine the technical feasibility of developing a\npelletizing industry in the state of Chihuahua, Mexico.\n    Fecha de publicaci\u00f3n: 2011\n    Tipo de publicaci\u00f3n: Art\u00edculo\n    Idioma: Ingl\u00e9s\n    \u00c1rea de conocimiento: TECNOLOG\u00cdA DE LA CONSERVACI\u00d3N\n    Colecciones: Art\u00edculos de Congresos": [0.03224129229784012, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03224129229784012, 0.09672388434410095, 0.03224129229784012, 0.1934477686882019, 0.03224129229784012, 0.0, 0.03224129229784012, 0.03224129229784012, 0.03224129229784012, 0.0, 0.06448258459568024, 0.09672388434410095, 0.03224129229784012, 0.06448258459568024, 0.0, 0.09672388434410095, 0.03224129229784012, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03224129229784012, 0.06448258459568024, 0.0, 0.09672388434410095, 0.03224129229784012, 0.0, 0.12896516919136047, 0.1934477686882019, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03224129229784012, 0.03224129229784012, 0.0, 0.06448258459568024, 0.06448258459568024, 0.0, 0.0, 0.12896516919136047, 0.09672388434410095, 0.06448258459568024, 0.0, 0.03224129229784012, 0.03224129229784012, 0.09672388434410095, 0.09672388434410095, 0.25793033838272095, 0.0, 0.03224129229784012, 0.1612064689397812, 0.06448258459568024, 0.03224129229784012, 0.03224129229784012, 0.06448258459568024, 0.06448258459568024, 0.5803433060646057, 0.09672388434410095, 0.06448258459568024, 0.0, 0.03224129229784012, 0.09672388434410095, 0.03224129229784012, 0.03224129229784012, 0.06448258459568024, 0.06448258459568024, 0.06448258459568024, 0.0, 0.0, 0.06448258459568024, 0.1612064689397812, 0.06448258459568024, 0.06448258459568024, 0.03224129229784012, 0.0, 0.06448258459568024, 0.06448258459568024, 0.0, 0.03224129229784012, 0.06448258459568024, 0.03224129229784012, 0.06448258459568024, 0.09672388434410095, 0.06448258459568024, 0.032241