pper sulphate. This bath was prepared based on a bath of electroless brass patented in Mexico, the\ncomposition of this bath using zinc oxide as a source of Zn+2 ions, a suitable complexing agent and a stabilizer, with an\nalkaline pH and a temperature of 75 \u00b0 C. The results indicate that we can control the colour of brass plating with Cu+2/Zn+2\nratio.\n    Fecha de publicaci\u00f3n: 2016\n    Tipo de publicaci\u00f3n: Memoria de congreso\n    Idioma: Ingl\u00e9s\n    \u00c1rea de conocimiento: OTRAS\n    Colecciones: Art\u00edculos de Congresos": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.11590011417865753, 0.07726674526929855, 0.0, 0.07726674526929855, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.23180022835731506, 0.0, 0.07726674526929855, 0.1545334905385971, 0.0, 0.07726674526929855, 0.03863337263464928, 0.1931668519973755, 0.07726674526929855, 0.03863337263464928, 0.11590011417865753, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.11590011417865753, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.07726674526929855, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.23180022835731506, 0.0, 0.0, 0.11590011417865753, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.27043360471725464, 0.0, 0.0, 0.07726674526929855, 0.03863337263464928, 0.1931668519973755, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.42496708035469055, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.07726674526929855, 0.07726674526929855, 0.0, 0.07726674526929855, 0.07726674526929855, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.11590011417865753, 0.27043360471725464, 0.07726674526929855, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.0, 0.1931668519973755, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.1545334905385971, 0.0, 0.0, 0.07726674526929855, 0.11590011417865753, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.07726674526929855, 0.03863337263464928, 0.11590011417865753, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.11590011417865753, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.0, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.07726674526929855, 0.07726674526929855, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928, 0.27043360471725464, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.07726674526929855, 0.0, 0.03863337263464928, 0.1545334905385971, 0.1931668519973755, 0.03863337263464928, 0.03863337263464928], "T\u00edtulo: Aluminum Mechanical Enhancing with Gr-Cu Nanoparticles Addition via High- Energy Ball Milling\n    Autores: JOSE MANUEL MENDOZA DUARTE Ricardo Mart\u00ednez S\u00e1nchez CALEB CARRE\u00d1O GALLARDO IVANOVICH ESTRADA GUEL\n    Colaboradores: \n    Nivel de acceso: Acceso Abierto\n    Licencia: Sin Derechos Reservados\n    Materia: Aluminum\n    Resumen: Aluminum (Al) composites, due to their low density and high strength have been applied in aerospace,\nground transportation and military industry [1]. These materials can be obtained by mechanical milling\nachieving a homogenous dispersion of reinforcing particles in the metallic matrix [2]. Recent studies\nhave obtained an increment on the mechanical properties with the addition of different reinforcing\nmaterials as nanotubes [3], graphenes [4] and carbon [5]. Additionally, mechanical properties were\nincreased using cooper (Cu) as reinforcement in Al composites [6]. On the other hand, graphite (Gr) is\nemployed as a reinforcing material because it is cheap, abundant and its particle size can be easily\nreduced.\n    Fecha de publicaci\u00f3n: 2016\n    Tipo de publicaci\u00f3n: Memoria de congreso\n    Idioma: Ingl\u00e9s\n    \u00c1rea de conocimiento: OTRAS\n    Colecciones: Art\u00edculos de Congresos": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.15269598364830017, 0.050898659974336624, 0.10179731994867325, 0.050898659974336624, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.050898659974336624, 0.050898659974336624, 0.0, 0.2035946398973465, 0.0, 0.2035946398973465, 0.101797319948673