 cataytic materials for hydrodesulphurization reactions of crude oil has been the transition sulfides, MoS2, know also  as the \"workhorse\" of the refinery industry. It has been proven by this and other research groups that the MoS2 laminar structure can increase its catalytic activity when promoted with cobalt or nickel. The location of active  sites seem to be at rim and edge sites on that particular laminar structure, as demonstrated using M\u00f6ssbauer spectroscopy  and x-ray techniques. However, due to maximun capability of this promoted systems, Co(Ni)/MoS2 to remove heterogeneous atoms (S, N, O) - a search for new catalytic  materials has curremtly been an ongoing activity in the HDS community.  Here, we will present the new family of ternary phase catalyst with special emphasis on their structural aspects, as revealed by aberration corrected (Cs) high-resolution transmission electron microscopy techniques, in an attempt to describe the nature of sites on this porous nano-rod like catalytic materials.\n    Fecha de publicaci\u00f3n: 2013\n    Tipo de publicaci\u00f3n: Objeto de congreso\n    Idioma: Ingl\u00e9s\n    \u00c1rea de conocimiento: PROCESOS QU\u00cdMICOS\n    Colecciones: Art\u00edculos de Congresos": [0.0, 0.04052204638719559, 0.04052204638719559, 0.04052204638719559, 0.08104409277439117, 0.04052204638719559, 0.24313227832317352, 0.12156613916158676, 0.0, 0.0, 0.08104409277439117, 0.08104409277439117, 0.04052204638719559, 0.08104409277439117, 0.2836543321609497, 0.04052204638719559, 0.0, 0.0, 0.16208818554878235, 0.0, 0.0, 0.12156613916158676, 0.04052204638719559, 0.0, 0.08104409277439117, 0.04052204638719559, 0.12156613916158676, 0.08104409277439117, 0.08104409277439117, 0.12156613916158676, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.08104409277439117, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.08104409277439117, 0.12156613916158676, 0.08104409277439117, 0.04052204638719559, 0.12156613916158676, 0.04052204638719559, 0.0, 0.0, 0.16208818554878235, 0.08104409277439117, 0.0, 0.12156613916